course: dictionary
lesson: 2149
title: Copy: the same, or to make the same
level: primary-5
stars: 1
explain: Copy can be a thing or an action. As a noun, a copy is a thing made to be the same as another one, like a copy of a photo. As a verb, to copy is to make something the same, or to do the same as someone else. «Each bottlenose dolphin has its own signature whistle, invented as a calf, which others copy to call it.» Here, other dolphins make the same whistle to call that dolphin.
explain: Look at the words around copy to see which job it does. In «the shop sold 150 copies», copies are counted: they are printed books or games of one kind. In «copy the sum from the board», copy is something you do: write the sum the same way. Ask yourself: is it a thing, or an action?
explain: Copy can also be a warning. «Changing a few words in someone else's writing does not make it yours; it is still copying.» In a test, copying another pupil's answers is cheating, and it is never allowed. «Film stunts must never be copied» because real stunt performers are trained, and even they can get hurt.
fact: A copy is a thing made to be the same as another one.
fact: To copy is to make a thing the same, or to do the same as someone else.
fact: «Copies» can mean printed books, newspapers or games of the same kind, like the 150 copies a shop sold.
fact: Dolphins remember old friends' whistles for over 20 years, so a copied whistle helps them call each other.
fact: In a test, copying another pupil's answers is cheating.
exercise: «The shop sold 150 copies of the new game.» What does copies mean here? | Bits of paper for drawing | Rules that everyone must follow | *Printed or made games of the same kind | Pages from a school book
exercise: Mia is told, «Copy the sum from the board into your book.» What does copy mean here? | Make it into a question | Rub it out | Hide it from the teacher | *Write it down the same way
exercise: «Changing a few words in someone else's writing does not make it yours.» What is this sentence telling you? | *Changing a few words is still copying | You can copy anything you like | Copying is always fine | Changing words makes writing yours
test: In a test, what is taking another pupil's answers? | A good idea | *Cheating | Fun | Helpful
test: Which phrase means to take words from one place and paste them somewhere else on a computer? | Copy out | Copycat | Copy down | *Copy and paste
exam: In «each dolphin has its own whistle, which others copy to call it», what does copy mean? | Throw it away | To forget | To sing very loudly | *To make the same whistle as another
